WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.177 --> 00:00:02.927
(dramatic music)

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:08.250
- Elon Musk is expected to
testify in a federal trial

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:12.270
that deals with tweets he sent in 2018,

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.570
regarding the possibility
of taking Tesla private.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.260
Elon Musk tweeted, "Am
considering taking Tesla private

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.750
at 420, funding secured."

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.360
He later followed up saying,

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.970
Investor support is confirmed.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.950
Only reason why this is not certain

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.800
is that it's contingent
on a shareholder vote."

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.100
Tesla's stock price closed up about 11%

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.700
the day that Mr. Musk sent those tweets,

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.383
and it later gave back those
gains and fell further.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.200
- Thank you all for
coming tonight, and I...

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.790
- The deal which would've been valued

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:51.540
at around $72 billion never materialized.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.380
The plaintiff has alleged
that Mr. Musk's tweets

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.800
were false material to investors

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.800
who relied upon them to
make trading decisions,

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.200
and that this class of investors

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.040
lost billions of dollars as a result.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.170
Attorneys presented opening statements

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.690
on January 18th, in the case.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:19.470
An attorney for the defendants
who include Mr. Musk,

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.110
Tesla, and members of
the board at the time

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:24.990
described the tweets as,

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:28.200
'Shorthand, made in the heat of the moment

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.360
that didn't differ materially

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.410
from the situation at hand, even though,

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:37.639
in some cases, they may have
been technically inaccurate."

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:38.880
(audience applauding)

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.830
The plaintiff is seeking damages

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.570
for investor losses

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:46.203
that Musk's tweets allegedly caused.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.357
The plaintiff said in a trial brief,

00:01:49.357 --> 00:01:51.030
"As a result of the turmoil

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.210
and the prices for Tesla
stock, options, and bonds

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.850
caused by Musk in Tesla's statements,

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.920
investors lost billions of dollars

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:03.480
from August 7th, 2018
to August 17th, 2018.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.880
The judge in this case has already ruled

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.000
that certain of Musk's
statements were untrue.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.780
That means that the key
questions left for the jury

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.780
include whether those statements
were material to investors,

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:22.233
and whether Musk knew
that they were untrue.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.053
Musk is expected to testify
as soon as January 20th.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.810
The witness lists indicate

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:35.010
that we may get to hear
from Tesla executives

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.770
and current and former board members

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:40.320
about what was going on inside the company

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:45.090
at this incredibly interesting,
chaotic time at Tesla.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:48.930
The trial is expected to
run for about three weeks,

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.550
through the beginning of February,

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:55.550
before being turned over to
the jury to decide the verdict.

00:02:55.797 --> 00:02:58.547
(tranquil music)

